{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZWa4JCMWPtfmNKkKKjr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SQA3Pa1rWUDFeM83jSsbAM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/attention_spectral_dynamics_20261030_140001_math02\ncat > literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n# Literature review (short, compiled by hand: the resource-finder stage was skipped)\n\n**Head importance and pruning.** Michel, Levy & Neubig (NeurIPS 2019, \"Are Sixteen Heads Really Better than One?\") rank heads by\nexpected loss change on removal and report removing up to 60% without loss depending on task and model; single ablations mostly have little effect. Voita et al.\n(ACL 2019) prune encoder heads with stochastic L0 gates (38/48 for 0.15 BLEU) and find specialised, confident heads go last. Neither uses a spectral\nor entropy threshold, so H3's criterion is new.\n\n**Spectra.** Linformer (Wang et al. 2020) reports long-tailed spectra of the trained Q-K matrix, more skewed in higher layers. \"Mind the Gap\" (arXiv 2410.07799) studies\nrank collapse at initialisation through a spectral gap. Effective rank is defined inconsistently: entropy of normalised singular values (Roy & Vetterli 2007),\nenergy thresholds, etc. So conclusions must be checked across definitions.\n\n**Information.** For deterministic nets MI with the input is constant (discrete X) or infinite (continuous X) (Saxe et al. 2018; Goldfeld et al. 2019), so any estimate reflects a\nregulariser. Binning-based estimates are unreliable (Goldfeld et al.). The noise channel plus pairwise-distance mixture bounds (Kolchinsky & Tracey 2017) give a well-defined quantity.\n\n**Lessons.** Use a defined noise scale, report it, and check the estimator ceiling; test against same-count pruning baselines; report the definitions.\nEOF\ncat > resources.md <<'EOF'\n# Resources\nThe pipeline's resource finder was skipped (`.neurico/pipeline_state.json`: `skipped: true`), so these were assembled in the experiment session.\n\n- AG News (`fancyzhx/ag_news`, local HF cache), SST-2 (`stanfordnlp/sst2`, local HF cache), CIFAR-10 (`uoft-cs/cifar10`, downloaded by `src/download_cifar.sh`).\n- Pretrained: `google-bert/bert-base-uncased` (local HF cache).\n- Papers: see `literature_review.md` and the references in `REPORT.md`. None downloaded.\n- Code: all written here in `src/`. No external repository used.\n- No LLM API key on this host; the study trains models locally and needs internals, so none was required.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write literature review and resources notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":121114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1744},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30402c77-19f2-456c-9b5e-2e376add52e6","uuid":"c19f9153-6f1d-444f-b95c-c0657c57793a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:17:08.273Z","request_id":"req_011CgZWa3vcwek9NMCJVs6td","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SQA3Pa1rWUDFeM83jSsbAM":{"command":"cd /data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/attention_spectral_dynamics_20261030_140001_math02\ncat > literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n# Literature review (short, compiled by hand: the resource-finder stage was skipped)\n\n**Head importance and pruning.** Michel, Levy & Neubig (NeurIPS 2019, \"Are Sixteen Heads Really Better than One?\") rank heads by\nexpected loss change on removal and report removing up to 60% without loss depending on task and model; single ablations mostly have little effect. Voita et al.\n(ACL 2019) prune encoder heads with stochastic L0 gates (38/48 for 0.15 BLEU) and find specialised, confident heads go last. Neither uses a spectral\nor entropy threshold, so H3's criterion is new.\n\n**Spectra.** Linformer (Wang et al. 2020) reports long-tailed spectra of the trained Q-K matrix, more skewed in higher layers. \"Mind the Gap\" (arXiv 2410.07799) studies\nrank collapse at initialisation through a spectral gap. Effective rank is defined inconsistently: entropy of normalised singular values (Roy & Vetterli 2007),\nenergy thresholds, etc. So conclusions must be checked across definitions.\n\n**Information.** For deterministic nets MI with the input is constant (discrete X) or infinite (continuous X) (Saxe et al. 2018; Goldfeld et al. 2019), so any estimate reflects a\nregulariser. Binning-based estimates are unreliable (Goldfeld et al.). The noise channel plus pairwise-distance mixture bounds (Kolchinsky & Tracey 2017) give a well-defined quantity.\n\n**Lessons.** Use a defined noise scale, report it, and check the estimator ceiling; test against same-count pruning baselines; report the definitions.\nEOF\ncat > resources.md <<'EOF'\n# Resources\nThe pipeline's resource finder was skipped (`.neurico/pipeline_state.json`: `skipped: true`), so these were assembled in the experiment session.\n\n- AG News (`fancyzhx/ag_news`, local HF cache), SST-2 (`stanfordnlp/sst2`, local HF cache), CIFAR-10 (`uoft-cs/cifar10`, downloaded by `src/download_cifar.sh`).\n- Pretrained: `google-bert/bert-base-uncased` (local HF cache).\n- Papers: see `literature_review.md` and the references in `REPORT.md`. None downloaded.\n- Code: all written here in `src/`. No external repository used.\n- No LLM API key on this host; the study trains models locally and needs internals, so none was required.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write literature review and resources notes"}}}
