{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZuse9aD8GmDsrN2ZSA4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SvhHoUr83ekQ6cb7idFYCQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/attention_spectral_dynamics_20261030_140001_math02\n.venv/bin/python -I - <<'EOF'\ns=open('REPORT.md').read()\nrep=[\n(\"The 0.3·log(n) threshold removed 63–96% of heads on AG News and CIFAR-10 at a cost of 19–45 pp.\",\"Under default initialisation, the 0.3·log(n) threshold removed 63–96% of heads on AG News and CIFAR-10 at a cost of 19–45 pp.\"),\n(\"| 3 / 6 / 12 | 5 / 8 / 5 | 5,600 |\",\"| 3 / 6 / 12 | 5 / 8 / 5 | 5,526 |\"),\n(\"| 6 | 5 | 5,600 | 92.1 |\",\"| 6 | 5 | 5,526 | 92.1 |\"),\n(\"| 6 | 8 | ~3,150 | 81.1 |\",\"| 6 | 8 | 3,156 | 81.1 |\"),\n(\"| 3 / 6 / 12 | 5 / 8 / 5 | ~7,500 |\",\"| 3 / 6 / 12 | 5 / 8 / 5 | 7,480 |\"),\n(\"Run times per job under contention: 3–39 min, BERT up to ~56 min.\",\"Training time per job under contention: 3–56 min.\"),\n(\"- Only BERT has any head above 0.6n (3%). This is present from the start, not a result of training.\",\"- Under rank_eff, only BERT has heads above 0.6n: 4% at the start and 3% at the end, in layers 1, 3, 4 and 6. These come from pretraining, not from this training run.\"),\n(\"- In default runs, the early rise is fast: most of it occurs in the first ~10% of training.\",\"- In default runs the rise is fast: 77–86% of the total rank increase occurs in the first 10% of training on AG News (L=3, 6, 12 and post-LN), 52–60% on SST-2 and CIFAR-10 at L=3, 6, and 45% on CIFAR-10 at L=12.\"),\n(\"Under this rule, the SST-2 pass depends on the short sequences (log n is smaller, and entropy reaches higher), not on the heads being identified as redundant.\",\"SST-2's normalised entropy ends higher (.32–.39 vs .26–.30 on AG News, with mean n 22 vs 46), so few heads fall below the line. This may be a sequence-length effect, which we did not test separately.\"),\n(\"Empirically, Î_BD stayed below this bound in all 2,400 checks.\",\"Empirically, Î_BD stayed below this bound in all 19,200 checks (every layer, noise scale and checkpoint). Î_KL may exceed it, since Jensen only gives Î_KL ≤ 2× the bound.\"),\n(\"Where b's CI includes 1 (order ε=1, 2; AG ε=1), the intercept is 1.4–5.5 nats, not ≈ 0.\",\"Where b's CI includes 1 (order ε=0.5, 1, 2; AG ε=1), the intercept is 1.4–5.5 nats, not ≈ 0.\"),\n(\"yet implied C grows from 7 to 180 on AG News and from 40 to 186 on the order task.\",\"yet implied C grows from 7 to 180 on AG News and, non-monotonically, from 40 to 186 on the order task.\"),\n(\"AG News plateaus by 40% of training, and the noise-free order task by 20%. Noisy order runs at n=8,000 were still rising at 80% of training (from 0.5 to 4.4 nats). Plateaus do not sit at H(Y|X).\",\"At n=8,000, AG News plateaus by 40% of training and the noise-free order task by 20%. The order task at η=0.2 was still rising late (0.5 nats at 20% of training, 3.8 at 60%, 4.4 at the end). Plateaus do not sit at H(Y|X).\"),\n(\"| cifar_L6_bigqk | .002 | .14 | 0.01 [0, .04] | 0.5% → 61% |\",\"| cifar_L6_bigqk | .002 | .14 | 0.01 [0, .04] | 0.4% → 60% |\"),\n(\"CIFAR-10: 0.5, 12, 32, 43, 54, 61%)\",\"CIFAR-10: 0.4, 14, 30, 42, 53, 60%)\"),\n(\"Also, at every checkpoint, deeper layers have lower rank than shallow ones. Linformer's report of more skewed spectra in higher layers agrees with this.\",\"Also, layer 1 has higher rank than the last layer at 95–100% of checkpoints in every configuration, though not always in strict order across intermediate layers. Linformer's report of more skewed spectra in higher layers agrees with this.\"),\n(\"*Small models:* BERT, far larger and pretrained, shows the same unimodal low-rank pattern with fewer heads changed by fine-tuning.\",\"*Small models:* BERT, far larger and pretrained, is also unimodal and mostly low-rank (dip p = .99). It starts peaked (row entropy ≈ 0.50) and its last layers lose rank during fine-tuning, which agrees with the ×3 arm.\"),\n]\nfor a,b in rep:\n    assert a in s, a[:50]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen('REPORT.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Spectral Dynamics of Attention Matrices During Training\n\nWe tracked per-head attention spectra over training in 68 transformers (text, vision, BERT fine-tuning) and ran 120 more with controlled H(Y|X), to test five claims on rank bifurcation, entropy shape, entropy pruning, an MI bound, and depth-accelerated collapse. Four claims fail as stated, and the pruning rule passes only on SST-2, where entropy did no better than random selection.\n\n## Key findings\n- **No bifurcation.** 0/68 runs meet the criterion under any of five rank definitions; heads form one population.\n- **Rank rises, it does not collapse, under default init.** Attention starts near-uniform (rank_eff/n ≈ .02–.09) and entropy climbs. Collapse appears only from peaked starts, and it deepens with depth (7% in layer 1 to 75% in layer 6 on AG News), at about 1.8× the speed rather than 3–5×.\n- **S < 0.3·log n is not safe for pruning.** It removes 63–96% of heads on AG News and CIFAR-10 for 19–45 pp loss. Entropy is still a useful ranking on CIFAR-10 (3–13 pp better than random) but not on text.\n- **I(A;X) ≤ H(Y|X) + O(1/√n) is false.** There is a simple counterexample, and at perfect accuracy measured information stays ≥ 1 nat (ε=2) with an excess that does not shrink with n. A valid variance bound is given in the report and held in all 19,200 checks.\n\n## Reproduce\n```bash\nuv venv --python 3.12 && UV_CACHE_DIR=$PWD/.uv_cache uv sync\nexport NUMPY_MADVISE_HUGEPAGE=0 HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1\nbash src/download_cifar.sh                         # AG News, SST-2 and BERT come from the HF cache\n.venv/bin/python -I src/prepare_data.py ag sst cifar bert\n.venv/bin/python -I src/test_units.py bert         # metric, MI-bound and BERT-port checks\n# one run:\n.venv/bin/python -I src/train.py --config ag_L6 --seed 0\n.venv/bin/python -I src/mi_run.py --task order --eta 0.2 --n 2000 --seed 0\n# whole grid (job list in logs/jobs/grid.txt; expects logs/jobs/ and results/{runs,mi}/):\n.venv/bin/python -I src/queue_runner.py logs/jobs/grid.txt 12 20\n.venv/bin/python -I src/analyze.py && .venv/bin/python -I src/figures.py && .venv/bin/python -I src/audit.py\n```\nThe full grid took about 5 hours on four heavily shared GPUs.\n\n## Files\n- `REPORT.md`: full report. `planning.md`: pre-registered criteria and deviations. `literature_review.md`, `resources.md`.\n- `src/`: `model.py` (encoder with attention access), `spectral.py` (metrics, MI bounds), `train.py`, `mi_run.py`, `prune_finetune.py`, `analyze.py`, `figures.py`, `audit.py`, `repro_check.py`, `queue_runner.py`.\n- `results/`: tables and raw per-run logs. `figures/`: report figures.\nEOF\ncat >> planning.md <<'EOF'\n6. Queue order changed mid-run so MI preceded the remaining depth repeats; GPU reservations lowered for MI (1.5→0.7 GB) and BERT (4→3 GB).\n7. ε=2 chosen as the H4 reporting scale after seeing the data, as the smallest scale free of the log M ceiling. All scales are reported.\n8. Rise-time ratios (time to peak) added for H5, because time-to-minimum is degenerate under default init.\nEOF\nls; du -sh results","description":"Apply audit corrections, write README and final deviations"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4979,"cache_read_input_tokens":215432,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4979},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30402c77-19f2-456c-9b5e-2e376add52e6","uuid":"e0e0b0fa-1f8e-48cb-b24d-b03b5ee9c5ae","timestamp":"2026-10-31T07:22:48.773Z","request_id":"req_011CgZusdpUpYrJdKxGLPP4t","wire_