n -I src/queue_runner.py logs/jobs/grid.txt 12 20\n.venv/bin/python -I src/analyze.py && .venv/bin/python -I src/figures.py && .venv/bin/python -I src/audit.py\n```\nThe full grid took about 5 hours on four heavily shared GPUs.\n\n## Files\n- `REPORT.md`: full report. `planning.md`: pre-registered criteria and deviations. `literature_review.md`, `resources.md`.\n- `src/`: `model.py` (encoder with attention access), `spectral.py` (metrics, MI bounds), `train.py`, `mi_run.py`, `prune_finetune.py`, `analyze.py`, `figures.py`, `audit.py`, `repro_check.py`, `queue_runner.py`.\n- `results/`: tables and raw per-run logs. `figures/`: report figures.\nEOF\ncat >> planning.md <<'EOF'\n6. Queue order changed mid-run so MI preceded the remaining depth repeats; GPU reservations lowered for MI (1.5→0.7 GB) and BERT (4→3 GB).\n7. ε=2 chosen as the H4 reporting scale after seeing the data, as the smallest scale free of the log M ceiling. All scales are reported.\n8. Rise-time ratios (time to peak) added for H5, because time-to-minimum is degenerate under default init.\nEOF\nls; du -sh results","description":"Apply audit corrections, write README and final deviations"}}}
