\n- I proved a replacement bound, based on attention variance, that held in all 19,200 checks.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- **Your derivation:** it wasn't in the workspace, so I tested the bound as written and read \"n\" as training-set size. A derivation with different assumptions could survive, but it would be a different claim.\n- **Post-hoc choices:** these are labelled exploratory in the report, and the deviations are logged in `planning.md`:\n  - the ×3 initialisation arm\n  - the rise-time ratios\n  - using noise scale ε=2 for reporting\n- **Literature:** the resource finder was skipped, so I compiled the review by hand from web searches, without reading full PDFs. The Kolchinsky & Tracey description is from memory, though a unit test confirms the bounds work.\n- **Weak spots:** SST-2 has only 436 test sentences, BERT has 3 seeds with very wide CIs, and fine-tuning after pruning was only run on the 6-layer default models. The bit-identical rerun check covered one configuration.\n- **Report audit:** checking the report against the raw logs caught several overstatements, which I corrected. `src/audit.py` reruns that check; the regression-scale correction was a separate manual fix.\n\nEverything is in `/data/summereunann/neurico-workspaces/attention_spectral_dynamics_20261030_140001_math02`; start with `REPORT.md`. Nothing was committed to git: no commit was requested, and git flags the repository root at `/data` as having dubious ownership.","ttft_ms":1864,"type":"result","duration_ms":2181548,"uuid":"90d78b6f-d8ce-4e63-842d-ae6e9bd555f9","ttft_stream_ms":1212,"time_to_request_ms":100,"first_content_frame_ms":1213,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":2}
